Restaurants=20
Cracker Barrel Cuts Debt as Restaurant Sales Slip

 Cracker Barrel reported fiscal fourth-quarter revenue of $849.3 million, d=
own=20
2.2% from a year earlier. Comparable restaurant sales fell 2.1%, while=20
comparable retail sales increased 0.7%.

 Net income rose to $12.2 million from $6.8 million, and adjusted EBITDA=20
increased to $62.1 million. That adjusted result included a $9.1 million ne=
t=20
benefit from tariff refunds.
MAIN POINTS=20
=E2=80=A2 Restaurant traffic and spending remained soft, with comparable re=
staurant=20
sales down 2.1%.

=E2=80=A2 Year-end debt fell to $337.2 million from $484.6 million.

=E2=80=A2 A sale-leaseback involving 26 stores generated about $77 million,=
 which was=20
used to reduce debt.

 The lower debt balance improves financial flexibility, but sale-leasebacks=
=20
replace owned real estate with future lease obligations. Investors should=
=20
separate operating improvement from the tariff-refund benefit and watch whe=
ther=20
restaurant sales stabilize without heavier discounting.

Source: Cracker Barrel =E2=80=94 September 23, 2026


